#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Explain how to use local Forge/Anvil (or Darwin MLX) with Cursor.
set -euo pipefail

base="${AI_BASE_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1}"
base="${base%/}"
model="${AI_MODEL:-forge}"

cat <<EOF
Cursor cannot keep cloud models (Grok / Composer / Claude) and a local
OpenAI endpoint in the same live picker. Override OpenAI Base URL is
global, and Cursor's backend cannot reach localhost without a public
HTTPS tunnel.

Recommended (alongside — already wired):
  • Cursor Agent / CLI  → cloud Grok (complex) / Composer (normal)
  • Continue panel      → local ${model} at ${base}
  • Pi / Hermes / Grok TUI / codex-local → same ${base}

Named profiles (stable; backend checkpoint can change later):
  • feather — DFlash 2, thinking off, greedy, 64k (fastest subagent)
  • forge   — thinking on, medium effort, 256k (daily / long sessions)
  • anvil   — thinking on, xhigh effort, 256k (hard / slow)
  Fast research with thinking: stay on forge and drop effort to low (Shift+Tab in Pi).

Open Continue in Cursor (sidebar) and pick Feather / Forge / Anvil.

Optional (Cursor Agent ON the local endpoint — cloud picker unavailable
while Override is ON):
  1. Expose ${base} via Cloudflare Tunnel / ngrok HTTPS
  2. Settings → Models → OpenAI API Key = local
  3. Override OpenAI Base URL = https://<tunnel>/v1
  4. Add custom model ids: feather, forge, and anvil
  5. Turn Override OFF before returning to cloud Grok/Composer/Claude

Health:
  curl -s ${base}/models | jq '.data[].id'
EOF

if curl -fsS --max-time 2 "${base}/models" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  echo
  echo "Local server: UP (${base})"
else
  echo
  echo "Local server: DOWN (${base})" >&2
  exit 1
fi
